; (0, 4) to (8, 4) bent toward (4, 0): B(t) = (8t, 4 - 8t(1 - t)), so the
; arch is symmetric about x 4, its ends on row 4 and its top on row 2
; (4 - 8/4). Walked it runs (0,4) (1,3) (2,3) (2,2) (3,2) ... and the
; middle of each L corner goes: row 3 keeps x 1 and 7, row 2 is x 2 to 6.
(new 9 5)
(curve 0 4 4 0 8 4 1)
